--   There exist a $\vartheta$-bounded configuration and a weight $\omega$ satisfying the discrete bounds (4), for every $\vartheta \in (0,\pi/2]$ and every real $\alpha$ and $R_0$.
--
--   This answers the first question a reader should ask of a formalized theorem quantified over configurations and kernels: whether anything satisfies the hypotheses. Without it, Theorem 1.3 could be vacuously true.
--
